  "adaptations": [
    "Source Tracker equality and exact error matching use host-local data, a keyed identifier and sanitized display. Tracker URLs, passkeys and arbitrary credentials do not cross into the worker. Verbose messages containing sensitive text are redacted.",
    "Native qBittorrent adds a label, and Transmission updates labels from a revalidated snapshot preserving existing values. Torrent deletion always preserves data. Uncertain acknowledgment remains fenced for the same stable task/effect. Independent downloader effects remain eligible when a different list read fails.",
    "Only configured Linux roots and explicitly mapped direct children may be cleaned. A complete selected downloader inventory, fresh references, physical local path ownership, a stable manifest and active-import checks are mandatory. Symlinks, service data, unsafe paths and uncertain effects fail closed. The App reconciles managed assets after confirmed removal.",
    "The host owns service lifetime, config, filesystem authority and installed instance identity. No custom page or plugin API is declared by this source. The actual form endpoint was tested, without a separate browser run for this standard schema."
  ],
  "review": {
    "reviewer": "/root/lark_finish_audit",
    "findings": [
      "Detailed logs restored; HTTP Tracker display aligned to netloc with redaction.",
      "Independent torrent effects no longer depend on another downloader's read success. File cleanup still requires the complete selected inventory.",
      "Final scan reset on each source-file pass addresses stale caches across scheduled downloaders."
    ]
  },
